# The build context for `packages/paywall-proxy/Dockerfile` (#5007).
#
# This file is Dockerfile-SPECIFIC: Docker reads `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore`
# beside the Dockerfile, so it applies only to
# `docker build -f packages/paywall-proxy/Dockerfile .`. There is deliberately
# no root `.dockerignore` — adding one would change the mcp-server image's build
# context (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, the MCP-server job).
#
# Patterns are relative to the build context root, which is the REPOSITORY ROOT.
# The image needs three workspace slices and nothing else, so this is a
# whitelist: exclude everything, re-include the three slices, then drop what the
# image rebuilds for itself.

*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.base.json
!packages

# Only the three packages the proxy's build touches: the SDK, the shared
# merchant payment core, and the proxy itself.
packages/*
!packages/sdk
!packages/merchant-payments
!packages/paywall-proxy

# Installed and built inside the image. These come last so they win over the
# re-inclusions above.
**/node_modules
**/dist

# Haven's own demo configuration is not part of the published kit. The image
# carries the kit's compiled output; a merchant supplies its own products file
# at `/config/products.json`, and `products.example.json` stays in the
# repository, where the README's Step 3 links to it. This is also why the #4892
# demo service keeps building from source (docs/operations/railway-services.md).
packages/paywall-proxy/demo
